AB  - Large Language Models (LLMs) have been integrated in various fields to support decision-making, including agriculture. LLMs can help farmers make more informed and timely decisions by processing and interpreting vast amounts of data, providing data-based recommendations that could significantly affect farm management and overall production. In this work, we aim to evaluate the potential of ChatGPT to provide targeted responses to kiwifruit farmers in the Greek language, focusing on kiwifruit plant diseases. Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is also employed in our evaluation towards enhancing the assistive capabilities and improving the model's performance, introducing KiwiAssist, a question-answering assistant for kiwifruit cultivation. Reported results demonstrated that RAG-based KiwiAssist outperformed the general purpose LLM and derived more precise and comprehensive answers. The mean relevancy score for KiwiAssist was 0.56, compared to 0.22 for the “vanilla” model. Results indicated that hybrid retrieval combined with query expansion and concise Greek answer generation could significantly improve factual accuracy in a specialized domain.
