AB  - A student’s career choice is one of their most difficult decisions. Many career guidance tools exist, but most of them provide only generic suggestions and fail to explain why a particular career fits someone [1]-[3]. To address this gap, we built an AI-powered career guidance system that combines machine learning predictions with a conversational chatbot [4], [5]. Our system uses an ensemble model consisting of LightGBM and CatBoost to predict the most suitable career roles based on a student’s skills, interests, certifications, and academic background [6], [7]. Unlike traditional models, we apply Sentence-BERT (SBERT) to understand the actual meaning of the skills entered by the user (not just the keywords) and use SMOTE [8] to balance the dataset so that less-common career options are not ignored. The predicted career roles are then passed on to a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) chatbot [9]–[11], powered by a Large Language Model (LLM). This chatbot explains top recommendations in simple language and gives relevant job descriptions. Our model achieves Top-3 accuracy of 98.78%, meaning that almost all students receive highly relevant job options [12], [13]. By combining accurate prediction with an intuitive chatbot interface, this system not only tells students what careers suit them but also explains why i.e. making career guidance more humane, accessible, and meaningful [14]–[16].
