AB  - Aim: The purpose of this research project was to create a LegalBuddy RAG-FAISS optimized chatbot for the purpose of providing improved access to legal services and increasing individuals' understanding of laws through the use of the models from the openrouter as the base engine. Research Methods and Material: This research involved two groups: Group 1 was the LegalBuddy Chatbot, while Group 2 was the BNS Mitra system. The study was conducted using a dataset extracted from the Government of India Code Portal, which was pre-processed using both bgl-small-en-v1.5 and FAISS-assisted search for establishing an accurate context to obtain the correct answers. Results: The results indicated that the LegalBuddy system greatly outperformed the BNS Mitra system on all performance metrics. The LegalBuddy System had an accuracy score of 0.989, a precision of 1.0 and an overall $F 1$-score of 0.995; the mean average accuracy was 0.99325. On the other hand, the BNS Mitra assured an accuracy score of 0.867 and had an overall F1-score of 0.929; the average score was 0.91575. Statistical analysis indicated that both models were statistically significant. Conclusion: It is concluded that the overall quality of responses provided by the LegalBuddy chatbot is superior and more consistent than that of the BNS Mitra chatbot, thus providing access to a complete understanding of the laws in the India legal system.
