AB  - As large language models (LLMs) continue to improve their capabilities in general tasks, they still face challenges in vertical domains with distinct characteristics (such as Chinese opera), including insufficient generalization ability for long-tail knowledge and high costs of domain-specific training. Although retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) methods can provide external knowledge support for models, they have limitations in capturing complex relationships across text chunks and documents. To address this issue, we propose a Graph-Interactive Retrieval-Augmented Generation framework (GIR), which leverages knowledge-graph-enhanced RAG to achieve precise knowledge-based question answering in the domain of Chinese opera (Shandong Bangzi). GIR consists of two core modules: (1) automatic construction of entity triple-text chunk knowledge graphs based on LLMs; (2) a graph-interactive retrieval mechanism that uses entity triples as indices and text chunks as targets. In addition, we manually constructed a Shandong Bangzi question-answering dataset for system evaluation. Experimental results show that GIR achieves significant improvements in both retrieval and answer generation for long-tail knowledge in vertical domains, demonstrating the effectiveness of this method in enhancing LLM performance in niche professional knowledge scenarios.
ER  - 

