AB  - InternBot is a multimodal conversational intelligence framework designed to address the growing need for accurate and context-aware career guidance systems. While recent advances in large language models have enabled conversational agents, many existing systems lack document grounding and multimodal reasoning capabilities. InternBot provides contextualized career guidance, internship recommendations, resume analysis, and document-aware advisory support by processing heterogeneous inputs, including text queries, speech-derived transcripts, and uploaded documents. The system employs a unified pipeline that integrates BERT-based semantic encoding, Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), and large language model (LLM) inference to enhance factual grounding, reduce hallucination, and improve personalized recommendations. InternBot was evaluated on a controlled benchmark comprising 30 multi-turn dialogues and compared against two competitive baseline systems. Experimental results across six evaluation metrics—dialogue success rate, response latency, user satisfaction, context coherence, BLEU, and BERTScore—demonstrate that InternBot achieves higher reliability, faster response generation, and superior contextual alignment.
