AB  - This study introduces an agentic multi-persona orchestration framework that leverages a structured intent inference technique along with parallel role-grounded reasoning and centralised supervisory synthesis. Contrary to the conventional approach of using a pre-routing system where a query is routed to a single agent for deliberation, this work routes each query to five different personas, i.e., Teacher, Parent, Senior, Friend, and Counselor. The proposed work uses an Intent-Driven Prior Scoring module within a four-tier routing cascade for probabilistic guidance without any bias towards a particular persona. The proposed work also utilises a supervisor for response evaluation based on relevance, role grounding, and coherence. The responses from the different personas are then synthesised to obtain a single response along with confidence. This work has been evaluated using a multi-label dataset, where the proposed framework has obtained 93.33% routing accuracy along with an 85.09% F1-score. The proposed work contributes to the area of agentic LLM orchestration by shifting the focus from single-path routing to parallel deliberation, enabling more contextually grounded and intent-aligned responses in complex dialogue tasks.
ER  - 

