AB  - Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) has become an effective paradigm for knowledge-intensive question answering. Agentic RAG further enhances this paradigm by incorporating autonomous agents to perform iterative reasoning and dynamic tool calling. However, existing systems often struggle with effective tool selection and usage, mainly because agents rely on static, generic context when calling tools. We propose TCA-RAG, a framework that improves tool calling through context adaptation. TCA-RAG accumulates tool-related experience at two layers: trajectory-layer experience that reflects how tools perform under specific query scenarios, and tool-layer experience that summarizes generalizable knowledge about each tool. During inference, the system retrieves relevant trajectory and tool experiences and integrates them into the agent’s context to guide efficient tool selection and usage. Experiments on multi-hop QA benchmarks show that TCA-RAG significantly improves answer accuracy and tool-calling efficiency compared with existing RAG and agentic baselines. The code is available in https://github.com/zirconiumnmlee/TCA.
ER  - 

