AB  - An AI-powered information assistant -Abhiyan is developed to streamline access to government schemes, especially for rural users who may lack technical knowledge. Its core purpose is to simplify data retrieval, enhancing information accessibility and bridging the digital divide. Utilizing advanced Natural Language Processing (NLP) and Large Language Models (LLMs), the developed chatbot can understand user queries, including those in regional languages, to provide relevant, userfriendly responses. Abhiyan leverages a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) framework, enabling it to pull real-time information from structured government notices and documents. By preprocessing and organizing data on various schemes, the system ensures accurate and efficient response delivery, addressing common inquiries like eligibility criteria and application processes. This work integrates LLMs for natural language understanding with RAG for data retrieval, creating a platform that promotes digital inclusion. Abhiyan's scalable infrastructure and ability to offer real-time updates make it a powerful tool for citizens and government agencies alike, empowering users with timely access to essential information on government schemes.
