AB  - The scarcity of Arabic-language educational tools tailored for university students, particularly in specialized fields like law and humanities, limits academic engagement and learning effectiveness. Mufakkir addresses this gap by providing an Arabic educational RAG-based chatbot designed to assist students with retrieving, summarizing, and interacting with academic content. The system is trained on a curated Arabic dataset of legal books collected from Ain Shams University, with synthetic question-context pairs generated for evaluation using an LLM. Mufakkir achieved 88% accuracy, 88 % recall, and $0.78 \text{nDCG} {@} 10$ on this benchmark. Its embedding model ranked first on the Arabic RAG Leaderboard with a score of 0.65, reflecting strong retrieval performance. In answer generation, it outperformed major LLMs such as DeepSeek, LLAMA, and Qwen, scoring 0.79 in Answer-Ground Similarity and 0.73 in Question-Answer Similarity. By combining fine-tuned embeddings, hybrid retrieval, and domain-specific evaluation data, Mufakkir delivers accurate, context-aware educational support.
