AB  - This paper presents an expert-knowledge-enhanced question answering and training assistance system for simulation training scenarios, where knowledge is dispersed, procedural constraints are strict, and response reliability is critical. The proposed method first organizes concept, rule, case, and procedural knowledge into a unified multi-source knowledge base. It then introduces a multi-evidence-constrained question answering mechanism that jointly leverages rule, procedural, and case evidence to guide large language model generation, improving answer accuracy and procedural correctness. In addition, a trustworthy output mechanism is designed through evidence consistency checking, rule conflict detection, and low-confidence control, enhancing the verifiability and traceability of generated responses. Based on these designs, a prototype system is implemented to support training preparation, in-process assistance, and post-training review. Experimental results show that the proposed method effectively improves the accuracy, procedural consistency, and trustworthiness of professional training question answering.
