AB  - The Viot Student Assistant System is designed to solve the common problems students face when searching for accurate and up-to-date academic information. In most colleges, important details such as timetables, syllabus documents, announcements, exam information, results, and placement updates are spread across websites, notice boards, WhatsApp groups, and PDF files. This makes information difficult to find and leads to confusion, delays, and repeated questions to faculty. To address this issue, Viot provides a centralized, intelligent mobile assistant that delivers instant, reliable answers using Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) with Large Language Models (LLMs). The system stores institutional documents in a vector database (Pinecone), enabling fast semantic search. When a student asks a question, the system retrieves the most relevant information and uses a generation model to produce a simple and clear response based only on verified college content. The backend is built using Ktor and the Gemini API, ensuring high performance for query processing. The frontend is developed as a native Android application to give students an easy and smooth user experience. Unlike general chatbots, Viot is domain-specific and trained only on college-related data, making the responses more accurate, consistent, and useful for academic needs.
